   "subject": "{Disarmed} Re: {Disarmed} Re: [distance-sampling] SE of shape and scale parameter estimates in R",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div>Elaine</div><br><div>Of course my math was rubbish in my previous answer.</div><br><div>Prof Buckland pointed me to an alternate way to get to your answer.  If you have your copy of Buckland et al. (2001) available, consult Eqn. 3.74 that deals with the variance of the natural log of a parameter estimate.</div><br><div><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/distance-sampling/attach/6a080b39c1772/Pasted%20File.png?part=0.1.1&amp;view=1\"></div><div>Wrestling with this expression, solving for var(D), you will arrive at</div><br><div><span style=\"color:purple\"><font style=\"font-size:14.6667px\"><font style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><a href=\"http://new.se\" title=\"new.se\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://new.se&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792473500310000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3xvkZPI9-zzito_HGSwAQK\">new.se</a></font></font></span><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125)\"><font style=\"font-size:14.6667px\"><font style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"> &lt;- estimate*sqrt(exp((se)^2)-1)</font></font></span></div><br><div><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125)\"><font style=\"font-size:14.6667px\"><font style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">where &quot;estimate&quot; is your estimate of sigma or beta (on the real scale) and se is the standard error on the natural log scale.</font></font></span></div><br><div><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125)\"><font style=\"font-size:14.6667px\"><font style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Try that out.</font></font></span></div><br><div><u></u><table cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tbody></tbody></table></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div><table cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"vertical-align:top;width:1px\"></td><td><div><strong>Eric Rexstad</strong></div><div>Senior Research Fellow, CREEM, Univ. of St Andrews, Charity SC013532</div></td></tr></tbody></table></div>"
