     2,
     "<blockquote><blockquote><div><div>Hello, </div><div><br></div><div>I have a question about the standard error for the parameters when estimating a detection function in R. I know when using Distance in R, the parameter estimates are given on the log scale. For my own analysis with a hazard rate key function (no adjustment terms), I would like to report report the estimates and standard errors of sigma and b (not log(sigma) and log(b) ). My question is, what is the SE column in the ddf information reporting? Is it SE(log(sigma)) and SE(log(b))? If so, how to I obtain the standard error of sigma and b? For reference, this is the output from my model: </div><div><br></div><div><div>Detection function parameters </div><div>Scale coefficient(s):  </div><div>            estimate        se</div><div>(Intercept) 2.330206 0.2733554</div><div><br></div><div>Shape coefficient(s):  </div><div>            estimate        se</div><div>(Intercept) 0.677233 0.2835995</div></div><div><br></div><div>Thank you much, </div><div>Elaine </div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div><br><div>--</div><div>You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;distance-sampling&quot; group.</div></blockquote></blockquote>"
